# Architecture boundaries

Preserve this pipeline. Do not collapse layers.

```
runtime configuration
  → transport
  → collector
  → parser
  → normalization / domain
  → policy filter
  → persistence
  → correlation / query
  → API / MCP
```

| Layer | May | Must not |
|-------|-----|----------|
| **Transport** | Speak a protocol; return raw text + exit/timeout | Know customer rules; parse business meaning; become a remote shell |
| **Collector** | Orchestrate **allowlisted** reads; classify completeness | Contain API/MCP/query logic; accept arbitrary commands from API, MCP, DB, or tenant config |
| **Parser** | Turn raw text into structures; tolerate **explicitly** known layouts | Do network I/O; mutate devices; treat malformed input as a reason to retry with a write |
| **Domain** | Canonical MAC/IP/interface IDs; observation semantics; provenance | Encode a named customer's topology |
| **Policy** | Drop out-of-scope observations (VLAN/CIDR/source/collector/interface) | Persist first and hide later in the API |
| **Persistence** | Store facts + time; upsert without deleting history | Silently decide “the truth” when evidence conflicts |
| **Correlation** | Join evidence; expose ambiguity | Invent certainty; hide conflicting observations |
| **API / MCP** | Expose the query layer | Reimplement correlation in a second copy |

Runtime secrets are injected outside Git (`secret_provider` + `secret_prefix` only in the database). See `docs/runtime-configuration.md` when that file exists, else `docs/architecture/overview.md`.

